  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="brands">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Which smart thermostat brands do you fit?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Every brand. Our engineers fit any smart thermostat or smart heating control, whether you buy it or we supply it.</p>
      <p>Not sure which one to buy? The table gives a quick guide. Call us with your boiler make and we will tell you what suits it.</p>
      <div class="brx-table-wrap">
        <table class="brx-table stk">
          <thead><tr><th>Brand</th><th>What it suits</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td data-label="Brand"><strong>Hive</strong></td><td data-label="What it suits">Most homes and most boilers</td><td data-label="Notes">Simple app. Versions for heating only, or heating and hot water.</td></tr>
            <tr><td data-label="Brand"><strong>Google Nest</strong></td><td data-label="What it suits">People who want the thermostat to learn their routine</td><td data-label="Notes">Uses a Heat Link receiver at the boiler. Can use OpenTherm on boilers that support it.</td></tr>
            <tr><td data-label="Brand"><strong>Tado</strong></td><td data-label="What it suits">Room-by-room control</td><td data-label="Notes">Pairs with Tado smart radiator thermostats.</td></tr>
            <tr><td data-label="Brand"><strong>Drayton Wiser</strong></td><td data-label="What it suits">Multi-room control, including homes with a cylinder</td><td data-label="Notes">Hub-based. Works with Wiser smart radiator thermostats.</td></tr>
            <tr><td data-label="Brand"><strong>Honeywell Home (T6, evohome)</strong></td><td data-label="What it suits">T6 for one zone. Evohome for larger, zoned homes</td><td data-label="Notes">Evohome can control each room separately.</td></tr>
            <tr><td data-label="Brand"><strong>Netatmo</strong></td><td data-label="What it suits">A simple, stylish thermostat</td><td data-label="Notes">Smart radiator valves are also available.</td></tr>
            <tr><td data-label="Brand"><strong>Danfoss</strong></td><td data-label="What it suits">Room-by-room control</td><td data-label="Notes">Known for radiator valves and smart radiator thermostats.</td></tr>
            <tr><td data-label="Brand"><strong>Worcester Bosch EasyControl</strong></td><td data-label="What it suits">Worcester Bosch boilers</td><td data-label="Notes">Made by the boiler maker for its own boilers.</td></tr>
            <tr><td data-label="Brand"><strong>Vaillant (vSMART, sensoHOME, myVAILLANT)</strong></td><td data-label="What it suits">Vaillant boilers</td><td data-label="Notes">Made by the boiler maker for its own boilers.</td></tr>
            <tr><td data-label="Brand"><strong>Baxi uSense</strong></td><td data-label="What it suits">Baxi boilers</td><td data-label="Notes">Made by the boiler maker for its own boilers.</td></tr>
            <tr><td data-label="Brand"><strong>Ideal Halo</strong></td><td data-label="What it suits">Ideal boilers</td><td data-label="Notes">Made by the boiler maker for its own boilers.</td></tr>
            <tr><td data-label="Brand"><strong>Salus and others</strong></td><td data-label="What it suits">Lower budgets</td><td data-label="Notes">Wired and wireless options. Ask us about any brand.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div class="brx-note"><p><strong>Already bought one?</strong> That is fine. We fit your own smart thermostat for £120, whatever the brand.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="included">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>What is included in smart thermostat installation?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Everything needed to get it working: a boiler check, proper wiring, removal of your old controls and app set-up.</p>
      <ul class="sg-ticks">
        <li>We check your boiler works with the thermostat, including OpenTherm or the boiler maker's own connection.</li>
        <li>We take off your old programmer or room thermostat.</li>
        <li>We wire the receiver to the boiler, or to your wiring centre on a system with a cylinder.</li>
        <li>We fit the thermostat in a good spot, away from radiators and direct sun.</li>
        <li>We test the heating, and the hot water if your model controls it.</li>
        <li>We set up the app on your phone and show you how to use it.</li>
        <li>Your old controls taken away, and a 12-month workmanship guarantee.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Prices include VAT. There is no call-out fee. If we find extra work, such as a new cable run, we tell you the price before we carry on.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="how">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>How does it work?</h2>
      <ol class="sg-steps">
        <li><strong>Call us.</strong> Tell us your boiler make and the thermostat you want, or ask us to help you choose. We give you a fixed price.</li>
        <li><strong>We check the boiler.</strong> On the day, we check the boiler and wiring before anything is changed.</li>
        <li><strong>Old controls off.</strong> We take off the old programmer or thermostat and make the wiring safe.</li>
        <li><strong>New controls on.</strong> We wire the receiver, fit the thermostat and connect it to your Wi-Fi.</li>
        <li><strong>Test and hand over.</strong> We test it all, set your schedule and show you the app. Most jobs take 1 to 2 hours.</li>
      </ol>
      <div class="brx-cta">
        <p><strong>Got a smart thermostat sitting in its box?</strong> We fit any brand for £120.</p>
        <a href={TEL} class="brx-btn">Call {PHONE}</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="which">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Which option is right for me?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">If you already have a thermostat, pick fit your own. If not, let us supply it. If your boiler is due a service, do both in one visit.</p>
      <div class="sg-cols">
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Fit your own: £120</h3>
          <p>Best if you have bought one, or spotted a good deal. You choose the brand. We check it suits your boiler and fit it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Supplied and fitted: from £249</h3>
          <p>Best if you want one less job. We help you choose, bring the right model and give you the exact price first.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-cols" style="margin-top:1rem;">
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>With a boiler service: £210</h3>
          <p>Best if the boiler has not been serviced this year. We service it for £120 and fit your thermostat for £90 more. See our <a href="/boiler-service-liverpool">boiler service</a> page.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Getting a new boiler?</h3>
          <p>Then you do not need to buy one. Every combi package on our <a href="/boiler-installation-liverpool">boiler installation</a> page includes a smart thermostat.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="boiler">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Will a smart thermostat work with my boiler?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Almost certainly. Nearly every working gas boiler can take a smart thermostat. The question is which one works best with it.</p>
      <figure class="sg-photo" style="max-width:360px;">
        <picture>
          <source type="image/webp" srcset="/images/jobs/boiler-smart-thermostat-fitted-480.webp 480w, /images/jobs/boiler-smart-thermostat-fitted-960.webp 960w" sizes="(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 360px" />
          <img src="/images/jobs/boiler-smart-thermostat-fitted-960.jpg" alt="Boiler and smart thermostat receiver fitted by our team in a Liverpool home" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="960" height="1280" />
        </picture>
        <figcaption>A boiler and smart thermostat receiver fitted by our team in Liverpool.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <h3>Combi boilers</h3>
      <p>A combi heats water when you turn on a tap. So the thermostat controls the heating. A heating-only model is usually all you need.</p>
      <h3>System and regular boilers</h3>
      <p>These have a hot water cylinder. Pick a model that controls the hot water too. We wire it into your wiring centre and zone valves.</p>
      <h3>OpenTherm and boiler brand controls</h3>
      <p>Some thermostats just switch the boiler on and off. Others talk to it, using OpenTherm or the boiler maker's own system. That lets the boiler run lower and steadier. We check what your boiler supports and tell you before you buy.</p>
      <div class="brx-note"><p><strong>Heating playing up already?</strong> A new thermostat will not fix a faulty boiler. If the boiler has a fault, book a <a href="/boiler-repair-liverpool">boiler repair</a> first. It is from £120 for the first hour, with no call-out fee.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="radiators">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Can you fit smart radiator valves?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Yes. We fit smart radiator valves from any brand for £65 per radiator, if you supply them.</p>
      <p>Smart radiator valves let you set each room on its own. Keep the spare room cool and the living room warm. They work with the matching smart thermostat from Tado, Hive, Drayton Wiser, Netatmo, Danfoss and others.</p>
      <ul class="sg-ticks">
        <li>Smart radiator valves fitted (you supply): £65 per radiator</li>
        <li>Standard TRV supplied and fitted: £65 each, or up to 6 for £295</li>
        <li>Radiator swap supplied and fitted: from £245</li>
      </ul>
      <p>See <a href="/radiator-valve-replacement-liverpool">radiator valve replacement</a> and <a href="/radiators-liverpool">radiators</a> for more. Got a few jobs to do? Our <a href="/small-plumbing-jobs-liverpool">small plumbing jobs</a> page shows how to fit them into one visit.</p>
      <div class="brx-note"><p><strong>Need an electrician too?</strong> If you want a new socket or spur for a hub, our partner firm <a href="https://www.idealelectricalsolutions.co.uk/">Ideal Electrical Solutions</a> can help.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</ServiceGuide>
